+### 6.7 `getPlayerLineage` as implemented in Step 4.8
+- `GET /api/v1/players/{player_id}/lineage`; same id grammar and error model as `getPlayer` (400 `INVALID_PLAYER_ID` with `instance` null, 404 only for a well-formed unknown id, 503 first when the service is unavailable, 405 for non-GET). `IMPLEMENTABLE_TODAY` in the contract.
+- Response: `player_id`, `identity`, `fields`, `meta`. **`identity` is built by the same function as in `getPlayer` and search** (`player_summary.build_identity`, extracted from `build_summary` with identical behaviour), so the AMBIGUOUS rules cannot diverge: `entity_kind`, `source_ids` (a source id only while its link is MATCHED/PROBABLE_MATCH) and `links` (confidence / matched_on only for MATCHED/PROBABLE_MATCH; no candidate). No `canonical_player_uid`, no uuid, no source record id appears anywhere (tripwires in `test_no_public_uid.py` cover this route too).
+- `fields`: every stored field value, one entry per source and field, sorted by `field_name` then source (= registry order today); disagreeing sources are BOTH listed, agreeing sources are NOT collapsed, nothing is merged, ranked or preferred. Values are the stored strings (byte for byte, empty string included); `dataset_version`, `fetched_at` (whole seconds UTC) and `is_current` are passed through (null included, keys always present); `data_origin` comes from the source registry, never from `dataset_version` (G2).
+- One query on `player_field_values` for EVERY player (new SQL `LINEAGE_FIELD_VALUES`, the only one, in `readmodels/definitions.py`): canonical players by `player_uid`, EA-only players by the unlinked EA rows (`source = 'ea_fc26'` and `source_record_id` = EA id). The second branch is restricted to `ea_fc26` on purpose, so an unlinked row of any other source (= a candidate) can never be selected. The values are read from the database rather than rebuilt from the in-memory index (exact strings and per-row provenance), so unlike the memory-served endpoints lineage answers 503 for an EA-only player when the database is lost.
+- Selection rule (the documented rule of every read model): the latest row per `(source, source_record_id, field_name)`, `fetched_at DESC, id DESC`; `is_current` is reported but never used to select; older rows (history) are not listed ("one entry per source"). Today no key has two rows and everything is current (a premise test fails on purpose when that changes).
+- **A source's values are shown only when it is `ea_fc26` itself or its link is MATCHED/PROBABLE_MATCH** (service filter on top of the SQL; unknown sources are never shown): the contract says candidate ids/names are never exposed. For a canonical player whose link is no longer MATCHED/PROBABLE (G12 scenario, none exists in the data) lineage therefore hides that source entirely, whereas `getPlayer` still shows a market value there; see G12.
+- States: EA-only -> 200, identity `EA_ONLY` with its real link statuses, and the six EA fields (one `ea_fc26` value each; nothing from Transfermarkt/Wikidata); the AMBIGUOUS EA-only player (Van Drongelen) -> the same, with the TM link `AMBIGUOUS`, `confidence`/`matched_on` null, no TM id and none of the candidate's (Mbappe's) values. Canonical -> EA fields + the linked sources' fields. Real data: 5 canonical players (EA + Transfermarkt, Haaland also 3 Wikidata fields) and 16,102 EA-only players, `preferred_foot` exists for everyone (EA only).
+- `meta.contains_sample_data`: true when a shown value comes from a sample source OR a shown id comes from a MATCHED/PROBABLE link against a sample (same rule as `getPlayer`; shared helper `identity_shows_sample_data`).
